Z||000000||2FAST4U||09-08-1999||07:08 AM||||Does anyone know of a reputable shop that can rebuild my 85 transaxle and beef it up enough to handle the rigors of SCCA SOLO events. Also need stronger axles and related parts..<P>THANKS MUCH<P>2FAST4U||||reg||
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||09-08-1999||11:55 AM||||I autocross my Fiero, and in my opinion, the tranny will be just fine, unless it's got something wrong with it. The only reason I can think you would need a stronger transaxle is if you plan on putting 300+ hp to the ground. I am running the Isuzu 5spd (everyone swears it's fragile) behind a strong running 2.8 for a few months now with no problems. If you have some money to dump into your autocrosser, get better shocks/struts, springs and bushings if you haven't yet. Just race it and replace what breaks. That's the cheapest method to my madness  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||
